{{!< default}}

<section class="shell page-surface custom-page" data-reveal>
    <header class="page-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Community promise</p>
        <h1>A place built on steadiness, dignity, and truthful care.</h1>
        <p class="page-dek">People come here carrying real tenderness. The tone of this site has to protect that. We want readers to feel safer after spending time here, not more hardened or more afraid.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="principles-grid">
        <article class="principle-card">
            <h2>No child-bashing.</h2>
            <p>Children are not the enemy. We do not write or gather in ways that reduce them to obstacles, villains, or proof that somebody failed.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
            <h2>No fear-selling.</h2>
            <p>We do not amplify panic for clicks. We name hard realities honestly, then help the reader move toward clarity and wise action.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
            <h2>No shame as a teaching style.</h2>
            <p>People learn more when they feel seen. Strong guidance can still be gentle, direct, and humane.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
            <h2>Belonging matters.</h2>
            <p>The family grows stronger when each person is treated like someone who matters, even in seasons of hurt, distance, or confusion.</p>
        </article>
    </div>

    <section class="custom-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">What we protect</p>
            <h2>The tone of safety is practical.</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="checklist two-column-list">
            <li>Language that lowers reactivity instead of escalating it</li>
            <li>Advice that respects the couple bond without erasing the child</li>
            <li>Permission to slow down and choose the next honest step</li>
            <li>Stories that feel human, grounded, and non-performative</li>
            <li>Room for grief, ambiguity, and mixed feelings</li>
            <li>Clear boundaries around cruelty, contempt, and scapegoating</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="custom-section note-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Important note</p>
        <p>This site can offer support and reflection, but it is not a crisis service and it is not a substitute for legal, clinical, or emergency help. If someone is in immediate danger, use local emergency resources right away.</p>
    </section>
</section>
